{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/772458-the-gaian-dance-a-3e-lunars-writeup","id":772458,"title":"The Gaian Dance - A 3E Lunars Writeup","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-23T12:31:04-08:00","id":772458,"title":"The Gaian Dance - A 3E Lunars Writeup","content":"Yes, you read this correctly. I'm working on a fan writeup for one of my few favorite splats, prior to the release of the book itself. I'm hoping that this will be roughly as well-known as terrifying argent witches was, considering its fame. But at the end of the day, here's what I have. Feel free to check up on it whenever you like, and I'll make an additional post here when it's well and fully done! Also feel free to ask questions.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11N-No1FQTMXPqSi8WiJAQKoE70P385OiJbT32JjIGxA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a> &lt;- Said writeup<br /> <br /> In general, this is meant to be on the scale of at least a full supplement if not a full splatbook outright. Hopefully this will let you lot play with lunars a bit more, before they're properly introduced into third edition.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Alright, alright. I admit it. The fluff was initially designed for a TAW-style 2E rewrite. HOWEVER, I have completely rewritten fluff and given the document a new title. Here's 2.0, with the mechanical fiddly bits from The Gaian Dance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2532,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","user":"BlitzKitty","date":". 01-26-2016, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","name":"BlitzKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T13:37:40-08:00","id":772497,"title":"","content":"Ooh, I will start looking at it when I get the chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","name":"Bulshock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T15:59:42-08:00","id":772581,"title":"","content":"I note that there's a lot more focus on the Primordials and origin stories than the rest of 3e, but I suppose there's not a hard rule against it. If it was me, though, I'd just give a paragraph or two to the backstory of Luna and the Lunars and use more space on Lunar achievements, inspiration, etc.<br /> Also, can you clarify Aspects a little? If I understand correctly, you get the latent abilities of, like, an eagle's Peck Out the Eyes, even when you're human? Also, maybe rename them to not clash with Dragon-blooded Aspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T16:31:36-08:00","id":772618,"title":"","content":"I agree that the focus on Gaia and Cytherea as related to Lunars and the mentions of other Primordials hurt the overall presentation, by stealing the spotlight away from Luna herself and <i>her</i> history and relation to her Chosen. This is something that should not happen.<br /> <br /> The initial mention of the chthonic baara in the Luna tale I liked, but I feel like some of the Lunar concepts and powers lean on it too much as a justification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T20:07:03-08:00","id":772751,"title":"","content":"Got a point there. It IS rather sparse when it comes to the lunars themselves. I'll take a moment to add some pages about the lunars in the modern era, their personages, and accomplishments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","name":"BlitzKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T18:33:58-08:00","id":816559,"title":"","content":"Bump, simply because I've updated it substantially to roughly twice the size of the original.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","name":"BlitzKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T22:14:22-08:00","id":817409,"title":"","content":"I'm reluctant to read 57 pages of text just like that. <br /> <br /> Could you summarize your approach, so that I can get an idea of whether this is my kind of thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T02:45:20-08:00","id":817485,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to focus on the practicalities of the Lunar Exalted, providing a framework for people to play them as usable characters. Giving setting information, as well as mechanical information. It's mostly a supplement to what's in core, and a few hooks here and there. Thematically, I want them to exist as iconoclasts. The solars are kinda mainstream in some ways, they're the big fellas who are popular and shiny. Not so with the Lunars, while they do have places where they're popular they don't naturally exist within the mainstream of civilization and society. If there's a place where they fit like a glove, it's likely a war dominion that they've engineered themselves. As said in the writeup, I want Lunars to exist in duality to the themes of the solar exalted. Embodying the positive aspects that they are not. Where the solars are strong consistency, they are adaptability that can fill the gaps. Where solars are refined skill, they are raw power. They're the other side of the solar coin, but the solars are the other side of the lunar coin equally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","name":"BlitzKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T16:53:38-08:00","id":818056,"title":"","content":"So your main mechanical themes are adaptability and brute force?<br /> <br /> What's it supposed to be like to play a Lunar under your rewrite?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T23:58:05-08:00","id":818246,"title":"","content":"Yep. Adaptability charms (One of three charm sub-categories) focus on boosting general capability, and filling holes in where the lunar's shapeshifting might falter. Protean charms focus on externalized shapeshifting, and Primal charms focus on playing up the connections to life and nature. What used to be knacks are mostly relegated to Protean and Adaptability charms, as the latter are generally more passive bonuses and the former are generally more active uses.<br /> <br /> Playing a lunar is supposed to feel weird. Unusual. It's supposed to feel like you're the one always outside of society, but always intermingling with it. These aren't the individuals who attempt to mold the world into their image as an end, when they do something resembling this in the form of war dominions it's very much a means. This is where they ultimately differ from the solar exalted: The solar exalted and particularly the Infernal Exalted (If I had my druthers, anyway) are world-changers. The lunars on the other hand, are more subtle and more effective. Yes, a lunar can try to be a conquering warlord and bring hell to the Realm and its satrapies. But really, a lunar who embraces their lunar-ness will know that they do that not for personal goals and wants, but as an agent of revolution pursuing an ideal. They're all about chasing that ideal, that intangible principle whereas solars are about chasing that concrete goal and powerful vision for the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","name":"BlitzKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T22:39:57-08:00","id":819701,"title":"","content":"Interesting. To me it is conceptually the other way around - solars are/were the one drawing power from principles and lofty ideas and bringing them to Creation, while Lunars had to anchor themselves with the here and now - people or territory, even if it meant something as broad as creation itself - as a counterweight to their protean spark and keeping themselves in balance. Too much baggage, and you end up like Ma-ha-Suchi, a bitter relic who cannot even freely change his shape. Too little, and you forget who you are undearneath all those masks, and end up as a Chimera. In my headcanon at least, the Chimerae were born not out of Lunars not being able to handle the Wyld, but of them forgetting or forsaking the things that they based their identity around.<br /> <br /> Okay, how do you see Lunar social, craft, and occult/lore charms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T23:35:27-08:00","id":819709,"title":"","content":"I'm not super-keen on the chasing-an-ideal angle, but the rest sounds decent. And Lunars are incoherent enough that no two visions are ever going to match.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I looked over the writeup. Skimmed the fluff, read the crunch a bit more carefully. My comments:<br /> <br /> -I like the &quot;Chimera are vulnerable to moonsilver&quot; bit.<br /> -Linking Abilities to faction seems a bit pointless.<br /> -Given Ex3's more-flexible approach to favouring so far...maybe characters should favour 2 Caste Attributes and 2 Attributes of their choice.<br /> -I think you should be allowed to be a Silver Pact member with little real hate for their enemies. They're not gonna turn away Lunars for being insufficiently hateful, are they?<br /> -Dunno about the Full and Changing Moon animas. They appear weak and strong respectively, and they seem Charm-ish to me. The No Moon anima's cool though.<br /> -Favors is an interesting background, but I really don't think you should limit people to canon NPCs.<br /> -Heart's Blood seems weak. A Merit dot is worth 3xp; while killing a tiger is an accomplishment, I wouldn't spend 9xp to avoid bothering.<br /> -I like Mask.<br /> -Blazing Pace seems too strong to me.<br /> -Entanglement is pretty cool, but can't you already grapple with your bare hands?<br /> -I like the weaker versions of Inhuman Palate, but the 5-dot version feels weak.<br /> -The last sentence before the Charms section doesn't make much sense.<br /> -I don't think Spine-Breaking Technique makes a good root for a Charm tree.<br /> -Burrowing Devil Strike looks insanely powerful. Heart-Seeking Fang might also be a bit much, I dunno.<br /> -I don't think Shattered Carapace Triumph should use Resources rating as a difficulty. Expensive =/= durable.<br /> -In general, this tree is too linear. Which naturally pushes the Strength prereqs up to an unfortunate level, cuts down on choices, and makes people buy Charms they don't want.<br /> -Silver Tides Surging, Wicked Hunting Maw, and Demon-Devouring Appetite all look too strong to me.<br /> -I like the idea of Overtaking The Wind. Not sure if it's balanced, though. And the reset condition seems unlikely to ever happen.<br /> -I would like Veteran Hunter's Acumen quite a bit if it was in Perception.<br /> <br /> PS: Have you read Irked's update? It's not a rewrite at all, but it still might be useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T23:17:12-08:00","id":820190,"title":"","content":"1: Thanks! Trying to draw a bit more on general werebeast lore, since chimerae are closer to the, 'Mindless Monster' take on werewolves and such.<br /> 2: Perhaps, perhaps. Was mostly going for flavor.<br /> 3: ...I'll think about that, though it does take a little bit away from the whole thing about lunars being category-based. It would give more freedom for concepts, though.<br /> 4: Eeeeeeh. It's less, &quot;HATE HATE HATE HATE HATE&quot; as per Kefka Palazzo and more, &quot;My attitude towards them is negative, to the point where it modifies my behavior&quot;. It's a more dispassionate interpretation of Ties, as it represents the willingness to regard the Sidereals and/or Realm as a threat, to go to war and risk your life against them.<br /> 5: Thanks for the input, I'll give them another look.<br /> 6: It's something you get whenever you complete a hunt ICly on a fairly powerful animal. One that's strong or distinct enough to warrant a statblock entry, anyway.<br /> 7: Thanks! It seemed like a good way to represent Lunars claiming human forms for subterfuge's sake.<br /> 8: ...Probably, yeah. It may be better to make it add dice and at the high-end version add double 9s.<br /> 9: Well, the main draw isn't so much the grappling as much as in the 3-dot version that it allows you to make one-off attacks at a relatively long range as far as unarmed is concerned. At 5-dots, the appeal is that you gain Reaching and Flexible, AND can use it as a poison vector on top of basic grappling ability. I contemplate changing that though, they seem more like two three-dot merits rather than one linear progression.<br /> 10: OK, good point. Sure, immunity to one poison is one thing. At the same time, it's... Not really /that/ great.<br /> 11: I'm mostly going off of the fact that it's a fairly low-level charm, if the lunar warrior statblock is any indicator. After all, DBT strikes me as more of a stamina charm given the precedent set by 2E's knacks.<br /> 12: I can see your point there, lunars will likely want to be broad where solars are deep. Flexibility, after all.<br /> 13: Changed silver tides surging, it now only extends melee attacks to short range rather than increasing all attacks by one range band. Gonna have to think about wicked hunting maw and demon-devouring appetite, though. Maybe move that last one up further.<br /> 14: I'll take a look at that, yeah. The reset condition needs work.<br /> 15: ...Hm. Perception... Maybe. I was thinking the mystical bent, the psychometry-alike approach would be intelligence but I can see perception almost as much if not moreso than intelligence.<br /> <br /> Finally no, I haven't. Post a link?<br /> <br /> EDIT: 4uk4ata, I see social as doing a bit of work with Inspire, as well as with Instill over other elements. Lunars aren't very much for socialize-related charms, unless they help lying and subterfuge. Certainly, they're not so much for the persona system or anything like that. They're too brute force and/or raw power for finesse and social niceties. The most I see there is first impressions being pulled off very well, and sheer glory overriding whether or not they're actually appealing to social norms and rules. As for lore/occult, I see some tricks that evoke tracking and hunting as well as occasionally more brutal methods like haruspicy (Divining the future from entrails).<br /> <br /> Craft is tricky, since Lunars never got much in the way of that in 2E so I'm kinda going in here blank slate. If I had my way with solars, I'd make them better able to do big and visible projects, but that's not so much what they have as much as general expertise. That being what it is, I'd make lunars really good at practical stuff, sometimes even making projects of minor value that nevertheless can be drawn out of the scenery within at least a scene or so. Maybe a thematic element of jury-rigging things together to produce something equally as potent if not better than a more involved session of crafting. I'm not so much talking about Craft (Genesis) from 2E. That was cool, but also a bit weird on multiple levels. At MOST potent, I'd look at the Telvanni from The Elder Scrolls for an example of what Lunars can do with improvisation and few materials. Growing buildings is extremely powerful, but also not out of the question for an E5 Lunar rocking craft charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2532,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","user":"BlitzKitty","date":". 01-31-2016, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","name":"BlitzKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T23:38:21-08:00","id":820193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlitzKitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/772458-the-gaian-dance-a-3e-lunars-writeup?p=820190#post820190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">11: I'm mostly going off of the fact that it's a fairly low-level charm, if the lunar warrior statblock is any indicator. After all, DBT strikes me as more of a stamina charm given the precedent set by 2E's knacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't trust the antagonist statblocks. They're designed to give a decent fight scene, not to provide a basis for a Charmset. I doubt that even the people who wrote them intend to use them when designing future splats.<br /> <br /> And anyway, having to buy a grappling Charm to buy totally-unrelated-to-grappling Charms is likely to cause feelbad moments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlitzKitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/772458-the-gaian-dance-a-3e-lunars-writeup?p=820190#post820190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally no, I haven't. Post a link?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\">Sure.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}